Subject: [PATCH] compose: per-field overrides on the command line

Eight switches set single fields of the composed profile:
--fingerprint-gpu-vendor, --fingerprint-gpu-renderer,
--fingerprint-hardware-concurrency, --fingerprint-device-memory,
--fingerprint-screen-width, --fingerprint-screen-height,
--fingerprint-timezone and --fingerprint-locale. The seed fills
everything else. A GPU override narrows the draw to a matching GPU
option, so WebGL limits and extensions still match the named renderer,
and a locale override applies before the speech voices are chosen. An
override the host cannot back, a screen smaller than --window-size, or
any override combined with --fingerprint=host refuses the launch with an
error. --fingerprint-explain reports each overridden field and the drawn
value it displaced.

--- a/base/apostate/compose.h
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.h
@@ -74,6 +74,31 @@
 // Write the composition report to stdout and exit.
 inline constexpr char kFingerprintExplain[] = "fingerprint-explain";
 
+// Per-field overrides. Each replaces exactly the field it names and leaves
+// every other surface to the seed, so an override is a correction to one
+// coherent device rather than a second, partial source of identity.
+//
+// None of these is page-visible. A page cannot read a command line, and every
+// one of them writes a value the catalogue could already have drawn into a
+// field the profile already carried -- the set of things a page can read is
+// exactly what it was, and with no override switch present nothing about a
+// launch changes at all.
+//
+// An override the host cannot serve, or that contradicts the capability
+// cluster it would have to sit on, is refused on stderr with the servable
+// alternatives named. Silently ignoring it is the one behaviour that must not
+// happen: the operator would then run a whole session believing a field was
+// spoofed when it was their own hardware.
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintGpuVendor[] = "fingerprint-gpu-vendor";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintGpuRenderer[] = "fingerprint-gpu-renderer";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintHardwareConcurrency[] =
+    "fingerprint-hardware-concurrency";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintDeviceMemory[] = "fingerprint-device-memory";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintScreenWidth[] = "fingerprint-screen-width";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintScreenHeight[] = "fingerprint-screen-height";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintTimezone[] = "fingerprint-timezone";
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintLocale[] = "fingerprint-locale";
+
 }  // namespace switches
 
 // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
