-BASE_EXPORT std::optional<Composition> Compose(const ComposeRequest& request);
+// Returns nullopt when the request itself is unusable (no seed, no platform
+// persona the tables know) and when a per-field override cannot be honoured.
+// The two are not the same answer and must not be confused: an unusable
+// request means inherit the host, while a refused override means the launch
+// asked for something specific and did not get it. `rejection`, when
+// non-null, is filled with the operator-facing reason in the second case and
+// left empty in the first, and a caller that passes one must stop the launch
+// rather than fall back.
+//
